# Build artifacts (Free Pascal)
build/
bin/
*.o
*.ppu
*.a
*.or
*.compiled
*.res
*.lps

# Local secrets and generated key material.
# Test keys are regenerated by `make fixtures` (tests/fixtures/gen_certs.sh);
# they are local only and never committed.
*.key
*.pem
id_*
.env
.env.*
*secret*
*token*
*.log

# Reference copy of upstream OpenSSL sources (see docs/openssl-reference.md).
# Downloaded locally, not part of the repository.
OpenSSL/

# Local reference copies of FPC/FCL units used while implementing the socket
# handler (sslsockets.pp, opensslsockets.pp, ssockets.pp). Not built or shipped.
docs/reference/

# Local agent configuration (may contain API keys). Never committed.
.subag/

# Editors / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.bak

# Embedded root certificates (task 19, docs/tasks/19-embedded-roots.md).
# The PEM snapshot and its metadata are the committed source of truth, so the
# global `*.pem` rule above must not hide them. The intermediate table and the
# resource script under build/roots/ are build artefacts and are ignored.
# src/tlsroots.res is the exception: tls.roots links it with {$R}, which FPC
# resolves at compile time, so a program that only puts src/ on its unit path
# (or a checkout on another host) needs the file to be present. It is committed
# and rebuilt by `make roots` when certs/ changes; .gitattributes keeps git from
# rewriting its bytes.
!certs/roots.pem
certs/roots.bin
build/roots/
!src/tlsroots.res
# Additional trusted roots supplied as extra generator inputs
# (task 20, docs/tasks/20-russian-trusted-root-ca.md). These PEM files are the
# committed source of truth for `make roots --extra ...`, so the global `*.pem`
# rule above must not hide them; the snapshot in certs/roots.pem and
# src/tlsroots.res are rebuilt from them.
!certs/extra/*.pem
